# A mode change while a turn runs (D4a follow-up): the turn's first write is
# judged in the harness's `auto`; while the model's second step is held open,
# Shift-Tab twice -- auto, full access, ask -- and the second write is put to
# the person rather than run. Ctrl-C refuses it and the turn goes on.
gateway permissions-midturn.json
wait 3
type write two files
wait 0.3
key Enter
wait 2
snap first-done
key BTab
wait 0.4
key BTab
wait 0.6
snap switched
wait 4.5
snap second-asks
key C-c
wait 1.5
# At a permission question Ctrl-C is the question's own deny and arms no
# exit hint (fx src/ui/input/runtime.zig:63@481104fd, `3 => .deny`; xfx
# shell.rs ctrl_c_at_a_question_answers_only_the_question_it_is_about).
# The turn ends on the refusal and the hint row is the hint's again, so
# halfway into the 3 s a hint armed in error is up, and `absent` fails
# the run on it; the check (capfile.py) counts that as no timer, so the
# snap stays where it was, at 3 s, rather than waiting a hint away.
absent press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 1.5
snap after-refusal
workls end
home end
